Fig. 10 illustrates the inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 in skeletal muscle 24 hours after injection. The top rows show that AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) co-injected with ovalbumin (OVA) leads to significant accumulation of Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages and MHCII+ cells (green), with intracellular Nano-11 visible within these cells. This indicates active uptake by these immune cells. Conversely, the bottom row, representing soluble OVA injection, shows few inflammatory cells and no significant uptake. This demonstrates Nano-11's ability to induce a local inflammatory response and target antigen-presenting cells in vivo.